  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BUILDING THE SUSTAINABILITY OF NEOTROPICAL GRASSLANDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners will build the ecological, economic and social sustainability of the conservation of Neotropical grassland dependent birds throughout Latin American through the development, documentation and dissemination of best management practices and the completion of the Latin American component of a Prairies to Pampas conservation business plan. This will be achieved by developing techniques and approaches to grassland conservation at key migration stopover sites; demonstrating and documenting responsible production approaches to natural grasslands conservation within rancher communities and policy environments in Latin America; building support for the conservation and sustainable use of natural grasslands through disseminating information; and engaging Latin American stakeholders in developing the conceptual model for the business plan, and integrating the plan with existing planning exercises.</narrative>
  </description>
